Error: Jet.UnknownContextField: `scheduler` isn't a context field or key
  --> Tests/UI/context_unknown_field.jet:7:14
    |
  7 |     #Context(scheduler: arena) { print("should not reach") }
    |              ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `#Context` sets `allocator`, `logger`, `on_stop`, `dir` and `env`, and the constants a package declares with `#ContextKey`
 Fix: Declare `#ContextKey scheduler: …` or write `#Context(allocator: …)`, `#Context(logger: …)`, `#Context(on_stop: …)`, `#Context(dir: …)` or `#Context(env: …)`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.UnknownContextField
